local 0125: a prompt row's bits never depend on how the prompt is split (prompt-cache resume == from scratch)

Why: since 0111 (lab 0204) the GDN gates b, a (fp16 weights of an EXL3 pack) take the fp16 mma prompt kernel
(b16._prompt_f16) only for pieces of >= 64 rows; shorter pieces fell back to prompt() (bf16 mma, another K order).
A prompt resumed from a cache point whose remaining piece (or the piece after a message-start stop) has < 64 rows
got other bits than the same rows prefilled from token 0: the 35B's resumed greedy replies differed in 1 of 5
scenarios (the old image b8baf4f2c717 was exact). Found with a bitwise split harness (every layer's expert
input/output rows, splits leaving 1..63 rows differ from layer 0; >= 64 equal). The v2 expert kernel itself is
row-exact (DET=1 grid sum).
What: prompt_pair takes the fp16 path at any row count (the Triton kernel masks rows; 1-63 rows cost one small
launch). Same bits as before for every piece of >= 64 rows, so long prompts and decode are unchanged.
Test: tests/cuda/test_prefill_p3.py::test_gate_pair_fp16_prompt_any_row_count.
Base: TensorFold 609ca419 + Flash recipe 0001-0010 + 0101-0124.
Rollback: TF_LOCAL_IMAGE=qwen36-35b-a3b-tensorfold-local:609ca419-7413bdfdc081 in .env.

